{
 "0001": {
  "title": "",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_593_01\" id=\"tag_17_593_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "strtol, strtoll — convert a string to a long integer",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_593_02\" id=\"tag_17_593_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/stdlib.h.html\">stdlib.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nlong strtol(const char *restrict</tt> <i>nptr</i><tt>, char **restrict</tt> <i>endptr</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>base</i><tt>);<br>\nlong long strtoll(const char *restrict</tt> <i>nptr</i><tt>, char **restrict</tt> <i>endptr</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int</tt> <i>base</i><tt>)<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_593_03\" id=\"tag_17_593_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "These functions shall convert the initial portion of the string pointed to by [I5]nptr[/I5] to a type [B6]long[/B6] and [B7]long\nlong[/B7] representation, respectively. First, they decompose the input string into three parts:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B6": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B7": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "An initial, possibly empty, sequence of white-space bytes",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5,
     3,
     1
    ],
    "text": "A subject sequence interpreted as an integer represented in some radix determined by the value of [I8]base[/I8]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5,
     5,
     1
    ],
    "text": "A final string of one or more unrecognized characters, including the terminating NUL character of the input string.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Then they shall attempt to convert the subject sequence to an integer, and return the result.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If the value of [I9]base[/I9] is 0, the expected form of the subject sequence is that of a decimal constant, octal constant, or\nhexadecimal constant, any of which may be preceded by a [CODE10] or [CODE11] sign. A decimal constant begins with a\nnon-zero digit, and consists of a sequence of decimal digits. An octal constant consists of the prefix [CODE12] optionally\nfollowed by a sequence of the digits [CODE13] to [CODE14] only. A hexadecimal constant consists of the prefix 0x or 0X\nfollowed by a sequence of the decimal digits and letters [CODE15] (or [CODE16]) to [CODE17] (or [CODE18]) with\nvalues 10 to 15 respectively.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE10": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'+'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE11": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'-'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE12": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'0'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE13": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'0'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE14": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'7'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE15": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'a'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE16": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'A'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE17": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'f'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE18": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'F'</tt>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "If the value of [I19]base[/I19] is between 2 and 36, the expected form of the subject sequence is a sequence of letters and digits\nrepresenting an integer with the radix specified by [I20]base[/I20], optionally preceded by a [CODE21] or [CODE22] sign. The\nletters from [CODE23] (or [CODE24]) to [CODE25] (or [CODE26]) inclusive are ascribed the values 10 to 35; only\nletters whose ascribed values are less than that of [I27]base[/I27] are permitted. If the value of [I28]base[/I28] is 16, the characters 0x\nor 0X may optionally precede the sequence of letters and digits, following the sign if present.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE21": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'+'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE22": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'-'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE23": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'a'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE24": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'A'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE25": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'z'</tt>"
     },
     "CODE26": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>'Z'</tt>"
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The subject sequence is defined as the longest initial subsequence of the input string, starting with the first non-white-space\nbyte, that is of the expected form. The subject sequence shall contain no characters if the input string is empty or consists\nentirely of white-space bytes, or if the first non-white-space byte is other than a sign or a permissible letter or digit.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     15
    ],
    "text": "If the subject sequence has the expected form and the value of [I29]base[/I29] is 0, the sequence of characters starting with the\nfirst digit shall be interpreted as an integer constant. If the subject sequence has the expected form and the value of [I30]base[/I30]\nis between 2 and 36, it shall be used as the base for conversion, ascribing to each letter its value as given above. If the subject\nsequence begins with a &lt;hyphen-minus&gt;, the resulting value shall be the negative of the converted value. A pointer to the\nfinal string shall be stored in the object pointed to by [I31]endptr[/I31], provided that [I32]endptr[/I32] is not a null pointer.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00015",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     17
    ],
    "text": "In other than the C [S33][[A34]CX[/A34]][/S33] [IMG35] &nbsp;or POSIX [IMG36] locale, additional\nlocale-specific subject sequence forms may be accepted.",
    "placeholders": {
     "S33": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG35": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG36": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     19
    ],
    "text": "If the subject sequence is empty or does not have the expected form, no conversion is performed; the value of [I37]nptr[/I37] shall\nbe stored in the object pointed to by [I38]endptr[/I38], provided that [I39]endptr[/I39] is not a null pointer.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00017",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     21
    ],
    "text": "These functions shall not change the setting of [I40]errno[/I40] if successful.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00018",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     23
    ],
    "text": "Since 0, {LONG_MIN} or {LLONG_MIN}, and {LONG_MAX} or {LLONG_MAX} are returned on error and are also valid returns on success,\nan application wishing to check for error situations should set [I41]errno[/I41] to 0, then call [I42]strtol[/I42]() or [I43]strtoll[/I43](),\nthen check [I44]errno[/I44].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I42": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I43": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00019",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A45][/A45]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A45": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_593_04\" id=\"tag_17_593_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00020",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, these functions shall return the converted value, if any. If no conversion could be performed, 0\nshall be returned [S46][[A47]CX[/A47]][/S46] [IMG48] &nbsp;and [I49]errno[/I49] may be set to [EINVAL]. [IMG50]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S46": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A47": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG48": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG50": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[S51][[A52]CX[/A52]][/S51] [IMG53] If\nthe value of [I54]base[/I54] is not supported, 0 shall be returned and [I55]errno[/I55] shall be set to [EINVAL]. [IMG56]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S51": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A52": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG53": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG56": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00022",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     5
    ],
    "text": "If the correct value is outside the range of representable values, {LONG_MIN}, {LONG_MAX}, {LLONG_MIN}, or {LLONG_MAX} shall be\nreturned (according to the sign of the value), and [I57]errno[/I57] set to [ERANGE].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I57": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00023",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A58][/A58]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_593_05\" id=\"tag_17_593_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00024",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "These functions shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00025",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00026",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "[S59][[A60]CX[/A60]][/S59] [IMG61]\nThe value of [I62]base[/I62] is not supported. [IMG63]",
    "placeholders": {
